From: Harshit Gupta <39994376+arelyx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:38:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/xenos: user clip planes and 3D textures

- PA_CL_CLIP_CNTL bits 0-5 enable the R300-style user clip planes and
  PA_CL_UCP_n (0x2388, four floats each) hold them, in clip space. That is
  what st passes without a GLSL vertex shader (fixed function, ARB vertex
  programs); gl_ClipVertex is still unhandled.
- 3D textures: linear layout as Xenia describes it (256-byte rows, slices
  of 32-row-aligned height, depth padded to 4, mips sized from the next
  power of two), DIMENSION_3D with the 11/11/10-bit size encoding, volume
  filters in dword 4, and a three-component fetch coordinate in ir2 (the
  third component was dropped from the register allocation, so a coordinate
  built in the shader lost r). Max 3D levels 11.

